<title>INDIA: Indian gold eases on poor demand, fresh offerings.</title>
<headline>Indian gold eases on poor demand, fresh offerings.</headline>
<dateline>BOMBAY 1996-10-01</dateline>
<text>
<p>Gold eased further towards the close on Tuesday amid sluggish physical buying coupled and fresh offerings, dealers said.</p>
<p>Gold biscuit (116.50 gramme) settled 100 rupees lower at 59,700 rupees per piece.</p>
<p>Silver opened lower on the back of weak trend in the world market but held steady at that level throughout the day on stray industrial support, dealers said.</p>
<p>The Bombay bullion market will be closed on Wednesday for a national holiday and reopen on Thursday.</p>
